Description
-----------

ohpvstatus shows the current energy flow of a house with a photovoltaic
system and a battery, read from an openHAB installation, in the VDR OSD:

  Battery SoC:        85 %      [|||||||||||||||||||||||||     ]
  PV Production:      4.32 kW
  PV Today:           18.47 kWh
  House Consumption:  612 W
  Battery Charging:   1.20 kW
  Grid Export:        2.51 kW
  Autarky today:      87.8 %

  Updated: 14:32:07

"PV Today" and the free lines at the end (here "Autarky today") are
optional, they are only shown if an item is given.

The plugin adds the main menu entry "openHAB PV Status". While the menu is
open the values are fetched again every update interval in the background.

  Red    fetch the values now
  Blue   setup page (update interval, unit, invert switches)
  Back   close


Requirements
------------

- VDR >= 2.4
- libcurl
- openHAB with the REST API (openHAB 2, 3, 4 or 5)
- for the SoC bar: a font that draws '|' as a bar segment, e.g. the
  vdrsymbols fonts, any other font shows plain '|' characters


Command line options
--------------------

Connection:

  -H HOST, --host=HOST    openHAB hostname or IP (default: 127.0.0.1)
  -P PORT, --port=PORT    openHAB port (default: 8080)
  --ssl                   use HTTPS instead of HTTP
  --ssl-verify=no         do not verify the SSL certificate (self-signed)
  --token=TOKEN           openHAB API token, only needed if openHAB does not
                          allow anonymous read access to the items. Create it
                          in the openHAB UI under your user profile, "API
                          Tokens". The token is sent as "Authorization:
                          Bearer". Note that VDR's plugin argument files are
                          usually readable by every user.

Items (default item names in brackets):

  --pv=ITEM               PV power (PVPower)
  --house=ITEM            house power (HousePower)
  --soc=ITEM              battery state of charge in % (BatterySoC),
                          --soc= without item hides the SoC line

Grid, choose one variant:

  --grid=ITEM             one item, positive = import, negative = export
                          (GridPower)
  --grid-in=ITEM          two items, import and export, both always positive.
  --grid-out=ITEM         Both must be given, otherwise --grid is used.

Battery, choose one variant:

  --battery=ITEM          one item, positive = charging, negative =
                          discharging (BatteryPower)
  --bat-in=ITEM           two items, charging and discharging, both always
  --bat-out=ITEM          positive. Both must be given, otherwise --battery
                          is used.

Optional lines, only shown if an item is given:

  --pv-today=ITEM         PV energy of today. The state may be a plain
                          number in Wh or a quantity in Wh, kWh or MWh. It is
                          shown in Wh or kWh like the power values (unit
                          setting in the setup menu).
  --line1=ITEM            free line 1, any item. A number is shown with the
                          unit openHAB sends ("87.8 %", "28.06 ct/kWh"),
                          a text state ("ON") as it is.
  --label1=TEXT           label of free line 1 (default: the item name).
                          Quote a text with spaces: --label1="Autarky today"
  --decimals1=N           decimals of a number in free line 1, 0-3
                          (default: 1)
  --line2=ITEM, --label2=TEXT, --decimals2=N
                          the same for free line 2

On Debian the options are set in /etc/vdr/conf.avail/ohpvstatus.conf,
otherwise with -P"ohpvstatus -H 192.168.1.10 --grid=MyGridItem ...".

If your items use the opposite sign convention (for example a battery that
reports charging as negative), use the invert switches in the setup menu
instead of changing openHAB.


Setup menu
----------

  Update interval (s)   1-300 seconds, default 10
  Unit display          auto (W below 1000 W, kW above), W or kW
  Invert PV/Grid/Battery/House
                        multiply the value by -1 before it is shown

The values are stored in VDR's setup.conf.


How the values are read
-----------------------

For every item the plugin reads

  http://HOST:PORT/rest/items/ITEM/state

over one HTTP connection. The state may be a plain number ("1234.5") or a
quantity with unit ("1.2 kW", "85 %"). W, kW, MW and mW are converted to W,
Wh, kWh, MWh and mWh to Wh.
The number is always read with a decimal point, independent of VDR's locale.

A test from the VDR machine shows what the plugin gets:

  curl http://HOST:8080/rest/items/PVPower/state

An item that does not exist, has the state NULL or UNDEF or needs a token
that was not given is shown as "n/a". "openHAB not reachable" means that
openHAB did not answer at all (wrong host or port, firewall, openHAB not
running), see the VDR log for the curl error.


Debian packages
---------------

Ready-made packages for Debian 13 (trixie) and VDR 2.8 are in the
vdr-portal.de APT repository (vdr-plugin-ohpvstatus).

The Debian packaging is kept in the branch debian/trixie of this
repository, on top of the release tag. To build the package yourself:

  git clone https://github.com/unf/vdr-plugin-ohpvstatus.git
  cd vdr-plugin-ohpvstatus
  git checkout debian/trixie
  gbp buildpackage

This needs git-buildpackage and vdr-dev of the VDR the plugin is built for.

